From: build fix
Subject: [PATCH] ssdk_phy_i2c: pre-4.16 i2c bus locking

i2c_lock_bus()/i2c_unlock_bus() and the I2C_LOCK_SEGMENT flag were introduced
in v4.16 when the i2c core gained per-segment locking. On kernel 4.4 only the
whole-adapter lock exists, and i2c_lock_adapter() is precisely what
i2c_lock_bus(adapt, I2C_LOCK_SEGMENT) was renamed from, so the mapping is
one-to-one with no behaviour change.

diff --git a/src/init/ssdk_phy_i2c.c b/src/init/ssdk_phy_i2c.c
index 8ac0fe6..af6bd65 100755
--- a/src/init/ssdk_phy_i2c.c
+++ b/src/init/ssdk_phy_i2c.c
@@ -23,6 +23,17 @@
 #include "ssdk_plat.h"
 #include "hsl_phy.h"
 
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 16, 0))
+/*
+ * i2c_lock_bus()/i2c_unlock_bus() and the I2C_LOCK_xxx segment flags arrived
+ * in v4.16. Before that the whole-adapter lock is the only one there is, and
+ * i2c_lock_adapter() is exactly what i2c_lock_bus(a, I2C_LOCK_SEGMENT) became.
+ */
+#define I2C_LOCK_SEGMENT             0
+#define i2c_lock_bus(_a, _f)         i2c_lock_adapter(_a)
+#define i2c_unlock_bus(_a, _f)       i2c_unlock_adapter(_a)
+#endif
+
 #define I2C_RW_LIMIT           8
 /******************************************************************************
 *
